// BT-3055: `^` inside a `to:do:` counted loop in an Actor class's *class*
// method used to emit a reference to an unbound `State` variable. A class
// method's Core Erlang signature is `(ClassSelf, ClassVars, Args...)` — there
// is no `State` parameter, only actor *instance* methods have one — but the
// counted loop's StateAcc pack/unpack helpers (`ThreadingPlan::generate_pack_prefix`
// and `ThreadingPlan::generate_exit_stateacc`) hardcoded `State` as their base
// whenever `CodeGenContext` wasn't `ValueType`, without checking for class
// methods specifically.
//
// Two class methods below exercise two distinct codegen paths that both hit
// this bug independently:
// - `runWithSelfSend` contains a self-send (`self foo`), which forces the
//   loop through the map-accumulator `StateAcc` fallback path
//   (`generate_pack_prefix`).
// - `runPlainSum` has no self-send or field write, so it takes the
//   direct-params fast path instead (BT-1275) — a distinct code path
//   (`generate_exit_stateacc`) with the same bug, not caught by fixing only
//   the fallback path.
//
// `Actor subclass:` (rather than `Object subclass:`) is used deliberately:
// an indirect `Object subclass:` ancestry only resolves to a non-actor
// `CodeGenContext` when the full class hierarchy is known at compile time
// (see `CoreErlangGenerator::is_actor_class`'s cross-file fallback), so it
// doesn't reliably reproduce this bug inside a full-stdlib compilation unit.
// `Actor` is recognized unconditionally, regardless of hierarchy completeness.

Actor subclass: BT3055Actor

  class foo => #FromAncestor

  class runWithSelfSend =>
    count := 0
    1
      to: 3
      do: [:i |
        count := count + 1
        ^self foo
      ]
    #wrong

  class runPlainSum =>
    total := 0
    1 to: 5 do: [:i | total := total + i]
    total
